          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 8.52,
          "en": "about a lot about Docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 8.52,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "what our different components are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 12.57,
          "en": "Now let's try to summarize everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 12.57,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "and also understand some new things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "inside the Docker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "So, what we have is when you open your Docker desktop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "or even if you work with Docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "basically as a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "So, let's say if you are a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "of course you're a user as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "So, if you're a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 28.11,
          "en": "you need to interact with Docker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 31.17,
          "en": "So, Docker is this big component here, a big box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "Now, this is where you have to talk to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "So, you cannot directly talk to Docker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "So, what we have in between is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "we have something called a client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 44.64,
          "en": "Now this is your Docker client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 44.64,
          "end": 48,
          "en": "Now, this Docker client actually talks to Docker, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 48,
          "end": 50.31,
          "en": "So, this is your Docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 50.31,
          "end": 53.4,
          "en": "and of course the client is also a part of a Docker software",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 53.4,
          "end": 56.58,
          "en": "because you don't separately install a client, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 56.58,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "When you install Docker, you get everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "So, yes, Docker client is also a part of Docker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 64.14,
          "en": "And now on the other side, we also connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 64.14,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "with the remote repositories, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "Or remote registry, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "So, basically, if you want any particular image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 72.75,
          "en": "you can simply search it on the registry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 72.75,
          "end": 74.28,
          "en": "and you can get it in your machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "That means we also have something outside this world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 79.38,
          "en": "which is called our registry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 79.38,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "Now, normally this registry can be public or private.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "Example, we have used the public repo, public registry,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 87.57,
          "en": "but this can also be a private registry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 87.57,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "So, let's say if you're working for a company",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 92.55,
          "en": "where they don't want to share their images to the world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 92.55,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "they can use a private registry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "So, this is connecting to this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.83500000000001,
          "en": "So, basically every time you interact with a Docker client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 99.83500000000001,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "Docker client connects with the Docker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "Now, (indistinct) when you say Docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "what exactly we have inside this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 109.44,
          "en": "Now, one thing we know in this particular thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 109.44,
          "end": 110.91,
          "en": "we'll be having images, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 110.91,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "So, we have worked with images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 112.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.6,
          "en": "In this we'll be having containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 114.6,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "We have worked with the containers as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "In this, we also have something called a network component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "to achieve any network stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "And then we'll also going to have here volumes. Okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "This is a part of it, but apart from this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 131.43,
          "en": "we also have one more thing here, which is called a daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 131.43,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "Now, this is your Docker daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "Now basically imagine Docker daemon as a background process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 138.727,
          "en": "So, every time you ask your client by saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 138.727,
          "end": 140.55,
          "en": "\"Hey, I want to get an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "I want to run a container.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 143.04,
          "en": "Who is responsible for it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 143.04,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "Who is responsible to get the image?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 147.6,
          "en": "Who is responsible to create, run the container?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 147.6,
          "end": 149.43,
          "en": "Because we are passing all those commands, right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 150.93,
          "en": "which we have learned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 150.93,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "Who is listening to it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "So, of course there should be a process which is running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "behind the scene, and that's your daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "And also there's something called an API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 161.91,
          "en": "So, basically, when you send a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 163.62,
          "en": "the request goes to the API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 163.62,
          "end": 165.097,
          "en": "and then this API knows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 165.097,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "\"Okay, this is what we need to do,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 168.09,
          "en": "with the help of Docker daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 172.26,
          "en": "And Docker daemon is responsible to get the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 172.26,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "run the container, configure the network,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "or if you want to connect with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "and also to create the volumes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "So, this is what basically happens behind the scene.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 182.557,
          "en": "So, whatever steps we followed initially when we said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 182.557,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "\"Okay, we want to pull the image.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 185.917,
          "en": "So, Docker daemon will go to registry by saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 185.917,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "\"Hey, I want the image, give it to me.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 190.44,
          "en": "So, all those process of pulling the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 190.44,
          "end": 192.93,
          "en": "running the container will be taken care by the daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 192.93,
          "end": 195.75,
          "en": "Now, this Docker daemon is also referred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 195.75,
          "end": 198.78,
          "en": "as dockerd, which is Docker daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 198.78,
          "end": 200.67000000000002,
          "en": "So, the process which running is dockerd.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 200.67000000000002,
          "end": 202.82999999999998,
          "en": "So, yeah, that's about the Docker architecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 202.82999999999998,
          "end": 203.663,
          "en": "which we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 203.663,
          "end": 205.89,
          "en": "We just try to summarize of whatever we have learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 205.89,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "One thing new is a Docker daemon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 210.21,
          "en": "And every time now when you, when you're on the Docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 210.21,
          "end": 213.06,
          "en": "you will come to know who is doing that behind the scene.",
